course: dictionary
lesson: 632
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. «Backbone» is one of these. In «The backbone is the line of bones down the middle of your back», it means a body part, also called the spine.
explain: «Maya is the backbone of the team, the player who keeps everyone going.» Here a backbone is not a bone at all. It is the most important part of something, the part that holds the rest up. Ask yourself: if I swap in «most important part», does the sentence still make sense? If it does, you have the right meaning.
explain: «Having backbone» means being brave and strong enough to do the right thing, even when it is hard. «Ella showed some backbone when she told the truth.» The clue is the word right: it shows the meaning is about courage, not about bones.
fact: The backbone is the line of bones down the middle of your back. It is also called the spine.
fact: «Backbone» can mean the most important part of something, the part that holds the rest up.
fact: Having backbone means being brave and strong enough to do the right thing.
fact: Animals with a backbone are vertebrates, such as fish, birds and mammals. Animals without one are invertebrates, such as insects, worms and jellyfish.
fact: «The Greenland shark is the longest-living animal with a backbone known, probably at least 270 years.»
exercise: «The backbone of the team is Maya, who never gives up.» What does backbone mean here? | *The most important part, which holds the rest up | A long, thin bone in the arm | The team's coach | The line of bones down your back
exercise: Which animal has no backbone? | A goldfish | *A worm | A lizard | A sparrow
exercise: «Ella showed some backbone and told the teacher the truth.» What does backbone mean here? | A bone in her back that hurt | A new game at school | *Being brave and strong enough to do the right thing | A line of players
test: «A tortoise's shell is joined to its ribs and backbone, so it can never leave it.» Why can a tortoise never leave its shell? | It is only joined on the outside, so it can slip out | Its shell is made of soft skin | It takes the shell off every night | *It is joined to its ribs and backbone, which are part of its skeleton
test: Which animal is a vertebrate, one with a backbone? | A jellyfish | A spider | An ant | *A goldfish
exam: «The Greenland shark is the longest-living animal with a backbone known, probably at least 270 years.» How long might it live? | Less than a week | About one day | *At least 270 years | Only ten years
